    # game/books.rpy:56
    old "Nostalgia is such a fickle thing. It entraps the heart and mind, lulling both into a sense of bittersweet, wistful longing. Then, just as soon as it comes, it is gone; a wisp in the wind, to return whenever fate may deem fit. Sometimes, it can take on the added effect of remembrance. Whether clear or vague, it leaves the mind curious, grasping at something it can or cannot recollect. Deja vu, as the phenomenon is termed first by Emile Boirac. A feeling so simple yet so mysterious. Yet, too, it is as memorable as ‘once upon a time.’ "
    new "Nostalgia is such a fickle thing. It entraps the heart and mind, lulling both into a sense of bittersweet, wistful longing. Then, just as soon as it comes, it is gone; a wisp in the wind, to return whenever fate may deem fit. Sometimes, it can take on the added effect of remembrance. Whether clear or vague, it leaves the mind curious, grasping at something it can or cannot recollect. Deja vu, as the phenomenon is termed first by Emile Boirac. A feeling so simple yet so mysterious. Yet, too, it is as memorable as ‘once upon a time.’ "

    # game/books.rpy:57
    old "Once upon a time, a time before technological advance and modernity, there was a rather interesting person. Their quirks, their whimsy, their charm, made them unique among their peers, their fellow man. A one-of-a-kind soul. Never again would it be replicated...at least, that is how things usually are. Fate is not so linear, so firm, as one might think. It is malleable, non-complacent - the smallest occurrence or entrance can change it. "
    new "Once upon a time, a time before technological advance and modernity, there was a rather interesting person. Their quirks, their whimsy, their charm, made them unique among their peers, their fellow man. A one-of-a-kind soul. Never again would it be replicated...at least, that is how things usually are. Fate is not so linear, so firm, as one might think. It is malleable, non-complacent - the smallest occurrence or entrance can change it. "

    # game/books.rpy:58
    old "A grand party was to be held at an estate near this individual; as were all about their settlement, they were invited to attend. Though their choice of costume and fashion kept them within social decency, it was not without the individual’s own special touch. The color combination, the silhouette, the very air about them was no short of spellbinding. Yet, no equally special attention was paid to them. Well, at least not entirely. There was one who, too, stood out among the rest. This person, cloaked in black, came upon this little light and asked for their company, their dance. "
    new "A grand party was to be held at an estate near this individual; as were all about their settlement, they were invited to attend. Though their choice of costume and fashion kept them within social decency, it was not without the individual’s own special touch. The color combination, the silhouette, the very air about them was no short of spellbinding. Yet, no equally special attention was paid to them. Well, at least not entirely. There was one who, too, stood out among the rest. This person, cloaked in black, came upon this little light and asked for their company, their dance. "

    # game/books.rpy:59
    old "Dance they did - around and around, dip and bow. The couple stepped and swayed until they could no more. And even then, chatter and laughter filled the space between them. A banter here, a quip there; a lovely giggle from the special one, a handsome smile from he who was darkly clad. Such a kinship could not come to an end with the coming dawn. The two found each other, again and again and again, without fail. "
    new "Dance they did - around and around, dip and bow. The couple stepped and swayed until they could no more. And even then, chatter and laughter filled the space between them. A banter here, a quip there; a lovely giggle from the special one, a handsome smile from he who was darkly clad. Such a kinship could not come to an end with the coming dawn. The two found each other, again and again and again, without fail. "

    # game/books.rpy:60
    old "A special bond between two individuals such as that could not go to waste. As most stories go, the companions soon formed a relationship that passed the barrier of friendship. This dark figure and sparkling light, both elated that the other reciprocated their affection. Ah, but there was a catch: a secret the man did hold. Never had he uttered it to another soul - not until then. He feared rejection, revulsion, terror from his darling love. Like the sun that brought about life for all on earth, the kiss bestowed by his lover warmed him, burned any doubt that remained in his heart."
    new "A special bond between two individuals such as that could not go to waste. As most stories go, the companions soon formed a relationship that passed the barrier of friendship. This dark figure and sparkling light, both elated that the other reciprocated their affection. Ah, but there was a catch: a secret the man did hold. Never had he uttered it to another soul - not until then. He feared rejection, revulsion, terror from his darling love. Like the sun that brought about life for all on earth, the kiss bestowed by his lover warmed him, burned any doubt that remained in his heart."

    # game/books.rpy:61
    old "  All good things must come to and end, eventually. A soul, no matter how special, will one day flicker and die. Their fleshy husk will wither and decay, slowly, until one day it breathes its last. This interesting person, who bound the man in love for eternity, one day came to meet their own maker. No amount of begging, bargaining, screams and tears, could prevent it. Like all mortals, his love’s soul awaited their own afterlife. "
    new "  All good things must come to and end, eventually. A soul, no matter how special, will one day flicker and die. Their fleshy husk will wither and decay, slowly, until one day it breathes its last. This interesting person, who bound the man in love for eternity, one day came to meet their own maker. No amount of begging, bargaining, screams and tears, could prevent it. Like all mortals, his love’s soul awaited their own afterlife. "

    # game/books.rpy:62
    old "But what if... What if, dear reader, there was one trick up his sleeve? A plot - a loophole, if you will. No one can stop the coming of Death, no one can. Though, perhaps, one can delay Death’s collection of a soul. If they were to hide it away, per se. If given such an opportunity to prolong your time with someone so special, would you? "
    new "But what if... What if, dear reader, there was one trick up his sleeve? A plot - a loophole, if you will. No one can stop the coming of Death, no one can. Though, perhaps, one can delay Death’s collection of a soul. If they were to hide it away, per se. If given such an opportunity to prolong your time with someone so special, would you? "

    # game/books.rpy:63
    old " Would you persist, even with the catch: your loved one would not remember their past life, and thus you. Your time spent together, the affection and care and passion you shared? Gone. Perhaps, if you are lucky, there are fleeting moments of recollection - that ‘deja vu’ aforementioned. A sense they’ve done something before. Read a book or poem, but they just can’t remember when; gazed upon glorious scenery or beheld spectacular, towering architecture and felt it familiar to the eye. Do you think you could make them remember?"
