    # game/books.rpy:303
    old "The night sky has always fascinated me, the vastness of it, how small it should make me feel is terrifying and beautiful at the same time. The stars which shine so brightly that I see as I stare up into the darkness may well have burnt out thousands of years ago, yet I can still see them sparkling above me. I still marvel at how we made constellations from the patterns we see in them, and how sailors used them to find their way home from sea."
    new "The night sky has always fascinated me, the vastness of it, how small it should make me feel is terrifying and beautiful at the same time. The stars which shine so brightly that I see as I stare up into the darkness may well have burnt out thousands of years ago, yet I can still see them sparkling above me. I still marvel at how we made constellations from the patterns we see in them, and how sailors used them to find their way home from sea."

    # game/books.rpy:304
    old "As a child I used to fight going to bed early or sneak out of bed to watch meteor showers or satellites moving across the sky, I no longer have to do that now, instead choosing to stay awake to watch events in the night sky because I simply want to. I can take a blanket and make a hot drink and sit outside and just enjoy the quiet stillness, I could stay out there for hours enjoying the cool air and the cloudless expanse above my head."
    new "As a child I used to fight going to bed early or sneak out of bed to watch meteor showers or satellites moving across the sky, I no longer have to do that now, instead choosing to stay awake to watch events in the night sky because I simply want to. I can take a blanket and make a hot drink and sit outside and just enjoy the quiet stillness, I could stay out there for hours enjoying the cool air and the cloudless expanse above my head."

    # game/books.rpy:305
    old "I have always preferred the moon over the sun, the softer glow that doesn’t burn my skin or make me squint my eyes closed due to the brightness. The night is quieter, more peaceful, more comforting where I am not busy rushing around with work or chores and I can just take time for myself to simply exist."
    new "I have always preferred the moon over the sun, the softer glow that doesn’t burn my skin or make me squint my eyes closed due to the brightness. The night is quieter, more peaceful, more comforting where I am not busy rushing around with work or chores and I can just take time for myself to simply exist."

