    # game/books.rpy:386
    old "Nat’s eyes opened as wide as possible, peering through the darkness of her room. Whatever was in there, she couldn’t see it, but she could feel it. It was back again, to torment her, to scare her, to ruin the precious hours of the night when we should feel the most at peace in restful sleep. She wanted to get up, to turn a light on and tell it to leave. But once again she found herself stuck in place, unable to move or speak or do anything, completely and totally petrified as if she just peered into the eyes of Medusa herself, making her bed feel more like a prison than a place of slumber."
    new "Nat’s eyes opened as wide as possible, peering through the darkness of her room. Whatever was in there, she couldn’t see it, but she could feel it. It was back again, to torment her, to scare her, to ruin the precious hours of the night when we should feel the most at peace in restful sleep. She wanted to get up, to turn a light on and tell it to leave. But once again she found herself stuck in place, unable to move or speak or do anything, completely and totally petrified as if she just peered into the eyes of Medusa herself, making her bed feel more like a prison than a place of slumber."

    # game/books.rpy:387
    old "Tears welled in her eyes as she felt each sharp pain on her body coming with no warning as she could not see the entity responsible for such agony. Again, and again and again, it went on for what felt like hours. She wasn’t sure how much more she could take, it felt like at any moment death himself would come for her if for nothing else but to relieve her of this torture. It had been weeks of these nightly visits from her invisible tormenting, she didn't know why it chose her, but she knew she couldn't hold on for much longer."
    new "Tears welled in her eyes as she felt each sharp pain on her body coming with no warning as she could not see the entity responsible for such agony. Again, and again and again, it went on for what felt like hours. She wasn’t sure how much more she could take, it felt like at any moment death himself would come for her if for nothing else but to relieve her of this torture. It had been weeks of these nightly visits from her invisible tormenting, she didn't know why it chose her, but she knew she couldn't hold on for much longer."

    # game/books.rpy:388
    old "Bracing herself mentally for the next lashing, she closed her eyes tight, her muscles tensing to prepare for the pain that she knew was coming. But this time, it didn’t. She waited, her eyes closed tight, sure that her attacker hadn't satisfied himself just yet. But When she opened them, she was surprised to see a swirling darkness in the corner of her room, so dark it looked like a mirror peering into the void itself. It was unlike anything she had ever seen before. Was this her assailant manifesting into its physical form? “Please, no…” she shuddered at the thought of it."
    new "Bracing herself mentally for the next lashing, she closed her eyes tight, her muscles tensing to prepare for the pain that she knew was coming. But this time, it didn’t. She waited, her eyes closed tight, sure that her attacker hadn't satisfied himself just yet. But When she opened them, she was surprised to see a swirling darkness in the corner of her room, so dark it looked like a mirror peering into the void itself. It was unlike anything she had ever seen before. Was this her assailant manifesting into its physical form? “Please, no…” she shuddered at the thought of it."

    # game/books.rpy:389
    old "Her imagination had barely a moment to run away from her when it was dragged back by a loud snap as the black hole disappeared before her eyes and in its place, on the floor was… a cat? No, this wasn’t just any cat. This was a black cat… A black cat that belonged to one of her best friends, Maz."
    new "Her imagination had barely a moment to run away from her when it was dragged back by a loud snap as the black hole disappeared before her eyes and in its place, on the floor was… a cat? No, this wasn’t just any cat. This was a black cat… A black cat that belonged to one of her best friends, Maz."

    # game/books.rpy:390
    old "“Smudge? What the hell are you doing here?” The words left her mouth before she even thought them, surprising herself to hear her own voice ring out through the darkness. The cat looked at her and tilted his head, casually flicking his tail back and forth. They held eye contact for a small moment, before Smudge looked back towards the center of the room. "
    new "“Smudge? What the hell are you doing here?” The words left her mouth before she even thought them, surprising herself to hear her own voice ring out through the darkness. The cat looked at her and tilted his head, casually flicking his tail back and forth. They held eye contact for a small moment, before Smudge looked back towards the center of the room. "

    # game/books.rpy:391
    old "His eyes flashed a bright red as he leapt into the air, a trail of absolute darkness following him and enveloping the entire room. Nat couldn’t see what was happening but she could hear the sounds of a fight; flesh tearing, blows landing, bodies being pushed into furniture. She sunk herself into her bed as deeply as she could so as to not get caught in the crossfire of the battle raging throughout her room, not moving a muscle until a loud growl burst into a roar of anguish and then was followed by a suffocating silence. The fight was over. "
    new "His eyes flashed a bright red as he leapt into the air, a trail of absolute darkness following him and enveloping the entire room. Nat couldn’t see what was happening but she could hear the sounds of a fight; flesh tearing, blows landing, bodies being pushed into furniture. She sunk herself into her bed as deeply as she could so as to not get caught in the crossfire of the battle raging throughout her room, not moving a muscle until a loud growl burst into a roar of anguish and then was followed by a suffocating silence. The fight was over. "

    # game/books.rpy:392
    old "Nat’s eyes darted around the darkness enveloping the room trying to see anything, any kind of hint of who was the victor. Slowly the familiarity of her room started to appear before her, moonlight pouring in through the window, illuminating the bright green eyes of the black cat sitting at the bottom of her bed."
    new "Nat’s eyes darted around the darkness enveloping the room trying to see anything, any kind of hint of who was the victor. Slowly the familiarity of her room started to appear before her, moonlight pouring in through the window, illuminating the bright green eyes of the black cat sitting at the bottom of her bed."

    # game/books.rpy:393
    old "“Oh, thank the gods,” she whispered, letting out a deep sigh of relief. Smudge stood up and stretched before making his way towards the top of the bed where he gently headbutted Nat’s arm. She ran her hand through his silky, black fur, feeling the soothing vibration of his deep purr as he paced back and forth alongside her. She smiled to herself, allowing the stillness in the room to wash over her, her muscles finally relaxing and releasing all the tension they had held just moments before."
    new "“Oh, thank the gods,” she whispered, letting out a deep sigh of relief. Smudge stood up and stretched before making his way towards the top of the bed where he gently headbutted Nat’s arm. She ran her hand through his silky, black fur, feeling the soothing vibration of his deep purr as he paced back and forth alongside her. She smiled to herself, allowing the stillness in the room to wash over her, her muscles finally relaxing and releasing all the tension they had held just moments before."

    # game/books.rpy:394
