    # game/books.rpy:500
    old "Today was another day I only caught myself long after sunset. Again, passed through distraction, searching for an escape I could never quite find. This was one more day I didn’t leave the house, spent in hiding. But I decided I could at least imagine I stepped outside today. The irritating need to do something — anything — having snapped my last thread connecting me to the reality of my bed beneath me."
    new "Today was another day I only caught myself long after sunset. Again, passed through distraction, searching for an escape I could never quite find. This was one more day I didn’t leave the house, spent in hiding. But I decided I could at least imagine I stepped outside today. The irritating need to do something — anything — having snapped my last thread connecting me to the reality of my bed beneath me."

    # game/books.rpy:501
    old "Sometimes, it’s okay to close my eyes to get my much-deserved rest, to stop pushing ever further ahead. Knowing that it’s time to dream while I wait for the Earth to twirl further about and for everything to catch up with my racing thoughts of possibilities."
    new "Sometimes, it’s okay to close my eyes to get my much-deserved rest, to stop pushing ever further ahead. Knowing that it’s time to dream while I wait for the Earth to twirl further about and for everything to catch up with my racing thoughts of possibilities."

    # game/books.rpy:502
    old "I would walk down the hill to meet the footpath bordering the towering Eucalyptus trees, passing by the last solitary streetlamp, then follow the path lit only by moonlight. Unlike in Earth’s nosier places, the stars would be able to surface for air here, and the trees would sing clearly to each other. And I would be able to think, to question, but maybe with less of a suffocating haze over my mind."
    new "I would walk down the hill to meet the footpath bordering the towering Eucalyptus trees, passing by the last solitary streetlamp, then follow the path lit only by moonlight. Unlike in Earth’s nosier places, the stars would be able to surface for air here, and the trees would sing clearly to each other. And I would be able to think, to question, but maybe with less of a suffocating haze over my mind."

    # game/books.rpy:503
    old "What does it mean to be alive? Is it having breath in my lungs, a spasming heart dragging blood through my veins, or pulses of electricity and chemicals screaming through my brain?"
    new "What does it mean to be alive? Is it having breath in my lungs, a spasming heart dragging blood through my veins, or pulses of electricity and chemicals screaming through my brain?"

    # game/books.rpy:504
    old "Some would argue that that isn’t enough to classify living, that I need to have a spark — a desire — for music, adventure, or my connections with other living beings. What happens if I had a spark and then lost it? Had it stolen away from me?"
    new "Some would argue that that isn’t enough to classify living, that I need to have a spark — a desire — for music, adventure, or my connections with other living beings. What happens if I had a spark and then lost it? Had it stolen away from me?"

    # game/books.rpy:505
    old "How do I find a spark? Even if it’s just one thing, one small hope. The universe expands far beyond the reaches of my touch with many things to latch on to and deepen my ties with. How do I choose which flames to feed when it all feels so far away, and my bonds are already threadbare?"
    new "How do I find a spark? Even if it’s just one thing, one small hope. The universe expands far beyond the reaches of my touch with many things to latch on to and deepen my ties with. How do I choose which flames to feed when it all feels so far away, and my bonds are already threadbare?"

    # game/books.rpy:506
    old "As I would brush past the trees bringing me the breath in my lungs, their gentle leaves like fingers reaching to cup my face and wipe away my very real tears, it would be hard to deny that there are innumerable connections. But how do I reach back—and should I?"
    new "As I would brush past the trees bringing me the breath in my lungs, their gentle leaves like fingers reaching to cup my face and wipe away my very real tears, it would be hard to deny that there are innumerable connections. But how do I reach back—and should I?"

    # game/books.rpy:507
    old "What is and isn’t safe isn’t always noticeable at first glance. Still, if I wait too long to peer into the dark, something that could’ve been beautiful could snap under the weight of my suspicions, its ends fluttering away in the breeze, never to be snatched back again."
    new "What is and isn’t safe isn’t always noticeable at first glance. Still, if I wait too long to peer into the dark, something that could’ve been beautiful could snap under the weight of my suspicions, its ends fluttering away in the breeze, never to be snatched back again."

    # game/books.rpy:508
    old "Pausing to choose whether to continue onwards or diverge off onto raw soil leading to a stream, the gentle trickle ushering in peace would also warn of danger, of suffocation. But peering into its dark waters, it would only ever reflect the desire drowned within myself—the talent buried below my surface."
    new "Pausing to choose whether to continue onwards or diverge off onto raw soil leading to a stream, the gentle trickle ushering in peace would also warn of danger, of suffocation. But peering into its dark waters, it would only ever reflect the desire drowned within myself—the talent buried below my surface."

    # game/books.rpy:509
    old "But what if I am scared to drown? To be so totally consumed by one’s passion takes dedication. And careful planning. Water will cling to my skin and soak in, altering my texture long after I have dried off. What happens if after the creek has dried up until a more favourable season, I find something that lights a greater fire in my heart than before, but now delicate threads slip through my wrinkled fingers? "
    new "But what if I am scared to drown? To be so totally consumed by one’s passion takes dedication. And careful planning. Water will cling to my skin and soak in, altering my texture long after I have dried off. What happens if after the creek has dried up until a more favourable season, I find something that lights a greater fire in my heart than before, but now delicate threads slip through my wrinkled fingers? "

    # game/books.rpy:510
    old "What happens when my brain and body differ from those around me, and I have no one to guide my search to the start of a thread made just right for me? How do I decide the right kind or colour of the material, learn how to wind each fibre together or even just overcome the boundaries placed before me to create?"
    new "What happens when my brain and body differ from those around me, and I have no one to guide my search to the start of a thread made just right for me? How do I decide the right kind or colour of the material, learn how to wind each fibre together or even just overcome the boundaries placed before me to create?"

    # game/books.rpy:511
    old "Say I decided I knew what to look for with certainty or stumbled upon it in an act of good fortune. I had found the stream on the off-beaten track, pushing through the trees’ warning arms that would keep my breath in my lungs but snuff out the light. I would notice my heart beating with purpose, my breaths coming faster in anticipation, and my brain flooding with bliss, informing me that what I had found was just right. How do I reach for it? Or them? How do I deepen my bonds to the world around me, especially to what I long for? How do I become comfortable, not overwhelmed?"
    new "Say I decided I knew what to look for with certainty or stumbled upon it in an act of good fortune. I had found the stream on the off-beaten track, pushing through the trees’ warning arms that would keep my breath in my lungs but snuff out the light. I would notice my heart beating with purpose, my breaths coming faster in anticipation, and my brain flooding with bliss, informing me that what I had found was just right. How do I reach for it? Or them? How do I deepen my bonds to the world around me, especially to what I long for? How do I become comfortable, not overwhelmed?"

    # game/books.rpy:512
    old "Looking around at all the vitality spiralling out from the stream, all its interconnected beating hearts and rustling leaves, I would find that I have even more questions. The hardest part comes when I’ve reached my home, my purpose. It’s not in the finding. How do I keep ahold of the fragile threads twirled around my fingers? Life has a way of wearing any threads bare, how do I reinforce them to withstand the weight of time? "
    new "Looking around at all the vitality spiralling out from the stream, all its interconnected beating hearts and rustling leaves, I would find that I have even more questions. The hardest part comes when I’ve reached my home, my purpose. It’s not in the finding. How do I keep ahold of the fragile threads twirled around my fingers? Life has a way of wearing any threads bare, how do I reinforce them to withstand the weight of time? "

    # game/books.rpy:513
    old "Hopefully, with my pyre blazing bright in my chest, I can find out. Forging more pieces of string from pure will alone and winding them all together to build a rope can be possible. Then, I can use that rope to drag myself ever further through my passions, feeding it to the flames until nothing is left to burn."
    new "Hopefully, with my pyre blazing bright in my chest, I can find out. Forging more pieces of string from pure will alone and winding them all together to build a rope can be possible. Then, I can use that rope to drag myself ever further through my passions, feeding it to the flames until nothing is left to burn."

    # game/books.rpy:514
    old "And as the Earth unspools on its doomed dance of passion, the sun will eventually demand the life left in the bones of the planets it forged, dragging them in by invisible ropes too massive to ignore. The universe will then ignite something new. Something bright and unignorable. By that time, the matter that makes me, me, and the substance that made my spark dazzle, both as they were, will have disappeared. Reformed into something or someone new, maybe. But I’ve realised that nothing will change that every moment I breathe, every beat of my heart, from that moment I found my spark or my spark found me, it will be what made me alive. Or at least, I now dream it will."
    new "And as the Earth unspools on its doomed dance of passion, the sun will eventually demand the life left in the bones of the planets it forged, dragging them in by invisible ropes too massive to ignore. The universe will then ignite something new. Something bright and unignorable. By that time, the matter that makes me, me, and the substance that made my spark dazzle, both as they were, will have disappeared. Reformed into something or someone new, maybe. But I’ve realised that nothing will change that every moment I breathe, every beat of my heart, from that moment I found my spark or my spark found me, it will be what made me alive. Or at least, I now dream it will."

